Why This Is Asked
Tests practical Azure design skills for low-latency, scalable dispatch with strict data isolation across cities.

Key Concepts
- Event Hubs with city-scoped consumers, Durable Functions for workflow state, Cosmos DB partitioning by city
- Low-latency data path and per-city caching in Redis; idempotent processing via dedup keys
- Auditing and observability through Cosmos logs and Application Insights; backpressure and DLQ handling

Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo: deduplicate and process ETA update
async function processEvent(evt) {
  const id = `dedup:${evt.eventId}`;
  if (await redis.exists(id)) return;
  await redis.set(id, 1, 'EX', 300);
  // compute ETA, persist, publish to Redis channels
}
```

